og — verified via browser_evaluate that 'QA Test Category Updated' no longer exists in DOM after deletion, and Income Categories count returned to 4.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-9\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Add Transaction dialog's Category dropdown offered Income categories (Sales Revenue, Consulting, Interest Income, Other Income) when Type=Income, and Expense categories (Office Supplies, Rent, Utilities, Salaries, Marketing, Travel, Software, Insurance) when Type=Expense; switching type reset category to \\\"Select category\\\". Selected category \\\"Consulting\\\" was retained and displayed on the created transaction row.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-11\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Toggled Tax Related switch on during creation; resulting transaction shows ✓ in Tax column.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-12\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Combined Type=Income + Category=Consulting + Date 2024-11-01..2024-12-31 + Search=\\\"Client\\\" narrowed correctly at each step (8→4→3→2 rows), and every resulting row satisfied all active criteria. Clicking Clear Filters restored the full 18-row transaction set with original totals (+$48,092.75 / -$36,485.99).\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-13\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Missing description/amount not identified to user\", \"actual\": \"Submitting the Add Transaction form with empty Description and empty Amount is silently blocked (no new row is added, row count stays at 19), but no error message, red border, aria-invalid, or any visible/inspectable indication is shown near the Description or Amount fields, and the aria-live region remains empty. The user is not told what is missing.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-15\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Invalid date range not rejected with explanation\", \"actual\": \"Setting From=2024-12-31 and To=2024-11-01 (start after end) does not produce any validation error. The filter silently returns zero results with a generic \\\"No transactions found / Try adjusting your filters\\\" message, without ever informing the user that the date range itself is invalid (start > end).\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-23\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Missing category not identified to user\", \"actual\": \"Submitting the Add Transaction form without selecting a Category (still showing \\\"Select category\\\") is silently blocked (no new row added), but no error message or field-level indication is shown to inform the user the category is required.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-24\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Deleting an in-use category is not blocked and does not require reassignment\", \"actual\": \"Deleted the 'Utilities' category which had 1 transaction assigned ('Electric Bill', -$285.00). The confirmation dialog itself stated 'Transactions using this category will not be deleted' — with no option to reassign or block the deletion. After confirming delete, the 'Electric Bill' transaction row was left with a blank/orphaned Category cell (verified via browser_evaluate: row text became 'Dec 5, 2024Electric Bill—-$285.00✓' with no category name between date and reference dash). This leaves data in an inconsistent state instead of blocking deletion or prompting for reassignment as required.\", \"evidence\": \"Delete confirmation dialog text: 'Are you sure you want to delete this category? Transactions using this category will not be deleted.' Post-delete transaction row category cell is empty.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-16\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Immediately after adding the current-month transaction (no reload), Dashboard Monthly Income/Net Profit and Recent Transactions updated to reflect it, and Reports page for August 2026 reflected the new total.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-17\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Toggled 'Tax Related' switch OFF on QA test transaction via Edit dialog and saved. Transaction row's Tax column checkmark immediately disappeared. Navigating to Tax Summary for year 2026 (the transaction's year) shows 'No tax-related transactions for 2026' and all totals $0.00, confirming the unmark correctly excluded the transaction from tax summary inclusion.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-18\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Categories page transaction counts/totals update live with underlying transaction data: (1) After the QA test transaction's category association was cleared via the Edit bug, 'Consulting' correctly showed 3 transactions/$10,800 (down from what would be 4 if the QA transaction were still counted), confirming counts recompute from actual transaction-category links. (2) Creating 'QA Test Category' immediately added it to Income Categories with correct 0 transactions/$0. (3) Deleting 'Utilities' category removed it from the Expense Categories list/count (8→7) immediately after confirmation, with no page reload needed.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-19\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Clicked 'Print Report' button on Tax Summary page (year 2024, with full data populated). No JS errors were thrown (console: 0 errors after click), no crash, no broken UI state — page remained fully rendered with all tax summary data intact after the print action.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-20\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Transactions table shows Date, Description, Category, Reference, Amount, Tax columns for every row, plus a footer with Total Income (+$48,092.75) and Total Expenses (-$36,485.99) for the current result set.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-21\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"After creating $500.25 income transaction dated today, Dashboard Monthly Income=$500, Net Profit/Loss=$500, Recent Transactions lists it first; Reports page (August 2026) shows Total Income $500.25, Total Expenses $0, Net +$500.25, matching the single transaction entered.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-22\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Chart Y-axis labels lack precision for sub-$500 values\", \"actual\": \"With a max monthly value of $500.25, both the Dashboard \\\"Income vs Expenses\\\" chart and Reports \\\"Daily Activity\\\" chart render 5 Y-axis tick labels as $0k, $0k, $0k, $0k, $1k. The intermediate non-zero tick values (~$125, $250, $375) are all displayed as \\\"$0k\\\", making them indistinguishable from an actual $0 value, and even the $500 top tick rounds to \\\"$1k\\\" rather than showing precise value.\", \"evidence\": null}]}"
